# The --host-globals manifest for bro's OWN bronze-compiled modules
# (bro_compile_js in ../CMakeLists.txt): observers.js, net_sync.js,
# image_gpu.js.
#
# This is NOT the app manifest. An app is compiled against what
# `bro-headless <appdir> --print-host-globals` prints — the registry of the
# binary that will run it — and that list cannot exist at build time, because
# bro-headless is the thing being built. So these modules are written to read
# what they need off `globalThis` at install time (`globalThis.document`,
# `globalThis.queueMicrotask`, ...) and name only three things as bare
# identifiers: the two every bronze program has, and the one host hook object
# C++ registers before the module runs. Keep it that way: a name added here
# must be registered by C++ BEFORE the module's entry runs, or the read is a
# fatal at first use.
globalThis
console
__bro_observers
